Key nvcc's --keep directory off the output object

The wrapper passes --keep, which writes intermediates named from the source
stem into the working directory. Under Bazel that is the one execroot every
action shares, so the PIC and non-PIC compiles of a source collide and ptxas
parses a .ptx the other nvcc is still writing. It presents as a parsing error
with the arch and line varying run to run, so it reads like anything but a
race. Each added -gencode widens the window.
